Author: Pepper Lebeck-Jobe <eljobe@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Mar 27 13:27:05 2025 +0100

    Multi redeem public (#313)
    
    * Add a method for redeeming a list of retryable ticket ids
    
    This will allow us to test that when many retryables are redeemed in the same
    block, that the execution client doesn't have any problems.
    
    Related to: NIT-3010
    
    * Add the gas cost to the call
    
    * Add the ability to create addresses to the RedeemAll method
    
    This change also renames the method to ReedeemAllAndCreateAddresses. The reason
    for the complexity of the commit is that we need to have a single top-level
    contract call that will cause many transactions to occur in the same block. Some
    of those transactions should cause accounts to be deleted, and others should
    cause accounts to be created.
    
    This way, we can tickle a bug in the current implementation of validation which
    occurs when account deletions and additions take place out of order and the
    validation logic isn't able to find a preimage for a particular account.
    
    * Convert tabs to spaces
    
    * format: yarn format
    
